1. GISLR 1st-place solution (network design, augmentation and preprocessing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

recognition/ffislr.py is a PyTorch port, with modifications, of the Google - Isolated Sign Language
Recognition (Kaggle, 2023) 1st-place solution by Hoyeol Sohn (hoyso48):
https://github.com/hoyso48/Google---Isolated-Sign-Language-Recognition-1st-place-solution
(licence verified 2026-10-11 at .../blob/main/LICENSE: MIT, "Copyright (c) 2023 hoyso48").

Modifications by the SignBridge contributors (2026): ported from TensorFlow to PyTorch; every face
input removed (lip and eye points blanked, face-mesh nose replaced by the pose nose, pose points 1-10
replaced by the pose nose); six pose points added; a single seed, no AWP; trained from scratch on the
team's own recordings. The demo checkpoint contains NO weights from the original solution (the
published weights were not used), and was not trained on GISLR or any other third-party data.

