The constants OFFSET_SW, R, SW and MID in recognition/ffislr.py (four small numbers that map our
shoulder-normalised coordinates into the original input's scale) were measured on 300 clips of the
Kaggle GISLR rerun set (dataset sohier/461054610546105, CC0: Public Domain; the underlying
collection is by the Deaf Professional Arts Network and the Georgia Institute of Technology). We
credit them although CC0 does not require it. No clip of that set is used in training.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. MediaPipe (landmark extraction)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Landmarks are extracted with MediaPipe (Google), Apache License 2.0:
https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe/blob/master/LICENSE
The holistic_landmarker.task model file is downloaded at first run and is not part of this
repository. Only pose and hand landmarks reach the classifier; the face is discarded.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Training data of the demo checkpoint
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The demo checkpoint is trained only on the team's own recordings (data/train: cosme, maya, nath,
roni; data/train_extra: talha, training only). The recordings are not part of this repository.
